From: LYW-30M local development <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: report valid RSSI and NSS 12.5 MPDU retry totals

Without peer PPDU samples the driver's RSSI EWMA is zero. Adding the
noise floor and marking SIGNAL_AVG overrides mac80211's management-frame
average with a fictitious -95 dBm. Leave the field unfilled in that case
so mac80211 can provide its own collected average.

NSS 12.5 reports MPDU retry attempts in retry.tx_mpdu_total_retry_count;
the legacy tx.retries field remains zero under observed load. Feed the
explicit total to nl80211 TX_RETRIES for that ABI. Keep the legacy mapping
for older firmware and do not add overlapping counters together.
This only changes host statistics, not rate control or NSS wire layouts.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -10109,11 +10109,14 @@
 	}
 
 	sinfo->signal_avg = ewma_avg_rssi_read(&arsta->avg_rssi);
-
-	if (!db2dbm)
-		sinfo->signal_avg += ATH11K_DEFAULT_NOISE_FLOOR;
-
-	sinfo->filled |= BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_SIGNAL_AVG);
+	/* NSS may not deliver peer PPDU samples. Do not replace mac80211's
+	 * collected RSSI with an uninitialized EWMA plus the noise floor.
+	 */
+	if (sinfo->signal_avg) {
+		if (!db2dbm)
+			sinfo->signal_avg += ATH11K_DEFAULT_NOISE_FLOOR;
+		sinfo->filled |= BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_SIGNAL_AVG);
+	}
 
 	if (arvif->ar->ab->nss.enabled)
 		ath11k_nss_update_sta_stats(arvif, sinfo, sta);
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -216,7 +216,12 @@
 			pstats->tx.tx_ucast_bytes +
 			pstats->tx.tx_bcast_bytes;
 		peer->nss.nss_stats->tx_bytes += tx_bytes;
+#ifdef NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_12_5
+		peer->nss.nss_stats->tx_retries +=
+			pstats->retry.tx_mpdu_total_retry_count;
+#else
 		peer->nss.nss_stats->tx_retries += pstats->tx.retries;
+#endif
 
 		for (j = 0; j < NSS_WIFILI_TQM_RR_MAX; j++)
 			tx_dropped += pstats->tx.dropped.drop_stats[j];
